# Frontend Next.js

- Use the App Router, server components where they help, and client components for interactive data views.
- Fetch through the typed SDK / TanStack Query. Do not scatter raw `fetch` calls in pages.
- Every data page must handle loading, empty, error, success, 403, no-results, pagination, search, filter, and sort.
- Use permission gates from the session payload. Hide actions the user cannot perform; still enforce 403 from the API.
- Prefer shared primitives from `packages/ui` and existing feature components. Do not create one giant page component.
- Forms use React Hook Form + Zod. Tables use TanStack Table.
- No fake KPI numbers. If the API returns zero, show an empty state.

```tsx
// BAD
<p>{data?.totalLeads ?? 1284}</p>

// GOOD
<KpiCard label="Leads" value={data.totalLeads} isLoading={isLoading} />
```
